#
# sqlplus 11.2's execute of `BEGIN open :rc for select level n, 'r' || level s
# from dual connect by level <= 3; END;` (its `exec`, #2466): one
# descriptor, a REF CURSOR (102) of one byte, then TTI_RXD and the value, a
# cursor id of 0 in four bytes.
# Captured 2026-11-06 through tools/capture_proxy.py: sqlplus 11.2 (instant
# client 11.2, x86-64 Linux) on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with SERVER=POOLED, the
# DRCP pool started. The TTC payload, without the packet's header, as
# `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by
# tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
